      'Start with administrative exceptions for one route: locked gates, missing access instructions, customer-requested schedule changes, technician photos awaiting review, and incomplete service notes. Leaks, electrical concerns, chemical exposure, unsafe conditions, suspected contamination, equipment failure, and customer disputes go to a qualified local owner. The remote output is a traceable handoff, not a field conclusion.',
